%%{init: {"theme": "default", "sequence": {"wrap": true, "noteAlign": "left", "noteMargin": 12, "actorMargin": 80, "messageMargin": 45, "boxMargin": 12}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    participant vLLM as vLLM / Bench Tool<br/>(Initiator Node)
    participant LMC_I as LMCache Engine<br/>(Initiator)
    participant IPU_I as MMG-400<br/>(Initiator IPU)
    participant WIRE as 400GbE
    participant IPU_T as MMG-400<br/>(KV Cache Node IPU)
    participant LMC_T as LMCache Server<br/>(KV Cache Node)
    participant DRAM as Registered DRAM<br/>(L1)
    participant SSD as NVMe Gen5<br/>(L2)

    Note over vLLM,SSD: Target flow (intended design).<br/>Page size P is a runner parameter (sweep 72 / 128 / 144 / 256 KiB) — all sizes below shown for P = 256 KiB.

    Note over vLLM,SSD: === RETRIEVE (Cache Lookup) ===

    vLLM->>LMC_I: retrieve(tokens)
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: hash tokens → chunk keys (BLAKE3)
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: allocate dest buffer in host DRAM<br/>RdmaWrapper.wrap() → (dst_rkey, dst_addr, 256KB)
    LMC_I->>WIRE: retrieve request (keys + dst descriptor) [ZMQ control]
    WIRE->>LMC_T: retrieve request

    LMC_T->>DRAM: hash table lookup

    alt L1 HIT (page in DRAM)
        DRAM-->>LMC_T: page found at addr Z
        LMC_T->>IPU_T: post RDMA Write (src=Z, dst=dst_addr, rkey=dst_rkey, 256KB)
        IPU_T->>DRAM: DMA gather (256KB)
        DRAM-->>IPU_T: page data
        IPU_T->>WIRE: RDMA Write (256KB)
        WIRE->>IPU_I: data arrives
        IPU_I->>LMC_I: DMA scatter to dest buffer (addr dst_addr)
        LMC_T->>WIRE: retrieve complete ACK [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: ACK
        LMC_I-->>vLLM: KV ready → DMA to GPU HBM

    else L1 MISS → fetch from L2
        DRAM-->>LMC_T: page not found
        LMC_T->>SSD: io_uring read (256KB)
        SSD-->>DRAM: page staged at addr Z (~80µs)
        LMC_T->>DRAM: index page (now hot)
        LMC_T->>IPU_T: post RDMA Write (src=Z, dst=dst_addr, rkey=dst_rkey, 256KB)
        IPU_T->>DRAM: DMA gather (256KB)
        DRAM-->>IPU_T: page data
        IPU_T->>WIRE: RDMA Write (256KB)
        WIRE->>IPU_I: data arrives
        IPU_I->>LMC_I: DMA scatter to dest buffer (addr dst_addr)
        LMC_T->>WIRE: retrieve complete ACK [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: ACK
        LMC_I-->>vLLM: KV ready → DMA to GPU HBM

    else TOTAL MISS (not in L1 or L2)
        DRAM-->>LMC_T: not found
        LMC_T->>WIRE: miss response [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: miss
        LMC_I-->>vLLM: miss → recompute KV
    end

    Note over vLLM,SSD: === STORE (Pull Model) ===

    vLLM->>LMC_I: store(tokens, kv_tensor)
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: DMA from GPU HBM → host DRAM, fence
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: RdmaWrapper.wrap() → (rkey, addr, 256KB)
    LMC_I->>LMC_I: compute BLAKE3(page) → digest D<br/>hold source MR registered until terminal ACK
    LMC_I->>WIRE: write intent (hash, rkey, addr, len, digest D, epoch) [ZMQ control, ~160B]
    WIRE->>LMC_T: write intent

    Note over LMC_T: Admission decision — four terminal or transitional states:<br/>ALREADY_PRESENT (dedup hit, idempotent success) · REJECT (over-quota / fenced epoch) ·<br/>QUEUE (no capacity, park under lease) · ACCEPT (capacity reserved, proceed to pull).

    alt ALREADY_PRESENT (dedup — key already committed under matching digest)
        LMC_T->>WIRE: ACK ALREADY_PRESENT (terminal, idempotent) [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: ACK ALREADY_PRESENT
        LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>store treated as success (identical retries collapse to the same outcome)
        Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — flow ends here.

    else REJECT (over-quota / fenced epoch / malformed intent)
        LMC_T->>WIRE: NACK (reason) [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: NACK
        LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>surface reject to caller (retry policy owned by initiator)
        Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — flow ends here.

    else QUEUE (no capacity yet — intent parked under lease)
        LMC_T->>WIRE: QUEUED (lease_id, lease_ttl) [ZMQ control]
        WIRE->>LMC_I: QUEUED — initiator keeps source MR pinned until ACCEPT/EXPIRE/CANCEL
        Note over LMC_T: Target holds intent in admission queue keyed by lease_id.

        alt LEASE EXPIRED (ttl elapsed, no capacity freed)
            LMC_T->>WIRE: EXPIRE (lease_id) [ZMQ control]
            WIRE->>LMC_I: EXPIRE
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>surface backpressure to caller
            Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — flow ends here.
        else INITIATOR CANCEL
            LMC_I->>WIRE: CANCEL (lease_id) [ZMQ control]
            WIRE->>LMC_T: CANCEL
            LMC_T->>WIRE: CANCEL ACK [ZMQ control]
            WIRE->>LMC_I: CANCEL ACK
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR
            Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — flow ends here.
        else DEQUEUE → capacity available (post-queue admission)
            LMC_T->>LMC_T: revalidate (epoch not fenced, digest D still bound, initiator alive)
            LMC_T->>WIRE: ACCEPT (lease_id) [ZMQ control — transition]
            WIRE->>LMC_I: ACCEPT (lease_id) — initiator keeps source MR pinned, proceed
            Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Continues into the shared ALLOCATE + PULL + VALIDATE + COMMIT block below (identical to immediate ACCEPT).

            alt L1 HAS FREE SLOT — no eviction needed
                LMC_T->>DRAM: allocate 256KB at addr Y (reservation held)
            else L1 FULL — evict LRU under two-phase reservation
                Note over LMC_T: Evicted slot stays UNAVAILABLE until L2 flush completes — on failure the LRU page is restored.
                LMC_T->>SSD: flush evicted LRU page (io_uring) — slot pending
                SSD-->>LMC_T: flush completion (success | failure)
                alt FLUSH OK
                    LMC_T->>DRAM: release evicted slot then allocate 256KB at addr Y (reservation held)
                else FLUSH FAIL — abort admission, no RDMA posted
                    LMC_T->>DRAM: restore LRU page (still resident, still indexed)
                    LMC_T->>WIRE: NACK (capacity — flush failure) [ZMQ control]
                    WIRE->>LMC_I: NACK
                    LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR
                    Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — addr Y was never allocated, no data loss.
                end
            end

            Note over LMC_T,IPU_T: Target pulls at its own pace — initiator MR still pinned
            LMC_T->>IPU_T: post RDMA Read (src=initiator:addr, dst=Y, 256KB)
            IPU_T->>WIRE: RDMA Read Request (64B)
            WIRE->>IPU_I: RDMA Read Request
            IPU_I->>LMC_I: DMA gather from registered DRAM
            LMC_I-->>IPU_I: page data
            IPU_I->>WIRE: RDMA Read Response (256KB)
            WIRE->>IPU_T: data arrives
            IPU_T->>DRAM: DMA scatter to addr Y (256KB)
            Note over LMC_T: Data landed — validate BEFORE commit
            LMC_T->>LMC_T: recompute BLAKE3(addr Y, 256KB) → D'<br/>compare against intent digest D
            alt VALIDATE OK (D == D')
                LMC_T->>DRAM: commit — publish (key → addr Y) in hash table
                LMC_T->>WIRE: store complete ACK (terminal) [ZMQ control]
                WIRE->>LMC_I: ACK
                LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>page committed and visible in L1 at target (L2 persistence is a separate lifecycle event)
            else VALIDATE FAIL (D != D' / read error)
                LMC_T->>DRAM: discard addr Y (do NOT publish)
                LMC_T->>WIRE: NACK (integrity) [ZMQ control]
                WIRE->>LMC_I: NACK
                LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>surface integrity failure (no retry from same MR)
            end
        end

    else ACCEPT (capacity available immediately)
        alt L1 HAS FREE SLOT — no eviction needed
            LMC_T->>DRAM: allocate 256KB at addr Y (reservation held)
        else L1 FULL — evict LRU under two-phase reservation
            Note over LMC_T: Evicted slot stays UNAVAILABLE until L2 flush completes — on failure the LRU page is restored.
            LMC_T->>SSD: flush evicted LRU page (io_uring) — slot pending
            SSD-->>LMC_T: flush completion (success | failure)
            alt FLUSH OK
                LMC_T->>DRAM: release evicted slot then allocate 256KB at addr Y (reservation held)
            else FLUSH FAIL — abort admission, no RDMA posted
                LMC_T->>DRAM: restore LRU page (still resident, still indexed)
                LMC_T->>WIRE: NACK (capacity — flush failure) [ZMQ control]
                WIRE->>LMC_I: NACK
                LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR
                Note over LMC_T,LMC_I: Terminal — addr Y was never allocated, no data loss.
            end
        end

        Note over LMC_T,IPU_T: Target pulls at its own pace — initiator MR still pinned
        LMC_T->>IPU_T: post RDMA Read (src=initiator:addr, dst=Y, 256KB)
        IPU_T->>WIRE: RDMA Read Request (64B)
        WIRE->>IPU_I: RDMA Read Request
        IPU_I->>LMC_I: DMA gather from registered DRAM
        LMC_I-->>IPU_I: page data
        IPU_I->>WIRE: RDMA Read Response (256KB)
        WIRE->>IPU_T: data arrives
        IPU_T->>DRAM: DMA scatter to addr Y (256KB)
        Note over LMC_T: Data landed — validate BEFORE commit
        LMC_T->>LMC_T: recompute BLAKE3(addr Y, 256KB) → D'<br/>compare against intent digest D
        alt VALIDATE OK (D == D')
            LMC_T->>DRAM: commit — publish (key → addr Y) in hash table
            LMC_T->>WIRE: store complete ACK (terminal) [ZMQ control]
            WIRE->>LMC_I: ACK
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>page committed and visible in L1 at target (L2 persistence is a separate lifecycle event)
        else VALIDATE FAIL (D != D' / read error)
            LMC_T->>DRAM: discard addr Y (do NOT publish)
            LMC_T->>WIRE: NACK (integrity) [ZMQ control]
            WIRE->>LMC_I: NACK
            LMC_I->>LMC_I: release source MR<br/>surface integrity failure (no retry from same MR)
        end
    end
